silm:instances_papers_09_minimal_category_theory_sections_07_composition_associativity_theorem_concrete_anchor_1_DomesticCat#domesticcat silm:hasLongDescription "The DomesticCat is the classification leg label; a typed class object distinct from Mittens; receives only the type leg, not the body-mass/microchip/care-process legs. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'DomesticCat', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
